  "url": "https://github.com/javaparser/javaparser/pull/5176",
  "visibleDescription": "No issue filed (CONTRIBUTING: \"If you know how to fix a problem, please fix it and open a pull request instead of opening an issue\").\n\nThe typed setters of the literal expressions assigned the `value` field directly instead of going through `setValue`, so they never sent a property change:\n\n- `StringLiteralExpr.setString` and `setEscapedValue`\n- `CharLiteralExpr.setChar`\n- `DoubleLiteralExpr.setDouble`\n- `IntegerLiteralExpr.setInt` and `LongLiteralExpr.setLong` (both deprecated)\n\nAs a result `LexicalPreservingPrinter` kept printing the old literal, while the pretty printer printed the new one:\n\nEach setter now calls `setValue(...)` and returns `this`, so the observers are notified and the same-value short-circuit from #4791 applies. One side effect: a `null` argument is now rejected by `setValue`'s `assertNotNull`. Before, `setString(null)` stored a `null` value (which then failed later, for example when printing) and `setEscapedValue(null)` already threw.\n\nChecks run (JDK 17, Maven wrapper 3.10.0):\n- `./mvnw -pl javaparser-core,javaparser-core-testing,javaparser-core-testing-bdd install`: 2910 tests (8 skipped) and 625 BDD tests, no failures.\n- `./mvnw -pl javaparser-symbol-solver-core,javaparser-symbol-solver-testing install`: 2165 tests (27 skipped), no failures.\n- `./run_core_metamodel_generator.sh && ./run_core_generators.sh`: no diff afterwards.\n\nNot run: the AppVeyor/CI matrix on other JDKs and operating systems."
